      "title": "Lora Wildcard Source Modes",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## IL — txt2img (Lora Wildcard Source - Test)\n\nSimplified workflow to test the new generic dynamic `LoraWildcardSource` node:\n\n- The Checkpoint loads model and clip directly into `LoraWildcardSource`.\n- `LoraWildcardSource` receives the base prompt from `PromptBuilder //Inspire` in the `base_prompt` input.\n- Select the `category` (style or pose). The second dropdown (`lora_wildcard`) will update dynamically by querying the Python backend.\n- It applies the corresponding LoRA and encodes the positive prompt directly.\n- The `model` and `conditioning` outputs go to the KSampler.\n- The modified `clip` goes to the negative prompt encoder.\n- The `lora_name` output goes straight to `SaveImage` as a prefix, automatically naming saved images with the LoRA name.\n\n*No need to use ImpactWildcardEncode or Text Concatenate.*"
      ],
      "color": "#223",
      "bgcolor": "#335"
    }
